#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# find_fit

#% text
# `find_fit(data, model, params, x)` gives the parameter values minimizing the sum of squared residuals of `model` against `data`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# `data` holds `[x, y]` pairs, rows `[x1, ..., xk, y]` for a list of variables, or plain values y at x = 1, 2, ...

#% item
# `params` lists symbols (starting at 1) or `[p, start]` pairs.

#% item
# Levenberg-Marquardt on machine numbers with the symbolic Jacobian; the result is a list of rules.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
find_fit([[1, 2.1], [2, 3.9], [3, 6.2]], p*x, [p], x)
#% output
#= [p -> 2.0357142857142856]

#% cell
find_fit([[0, 1.0], [1, 2.7], [2, 7.4], [3, 20.1]], a*exp(b*x), [[a, 1], [b, 1]], x)
#% output
#= [a -> 0.9983168020321654, b -> 1.0008344899743848]

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# Plain values:

#% cell
find_fit([1.0, 1.9, 3.2, 3.9], a + b*x, [a, b], x)
#% output
#= [a -> 9.289926551926663e-17, b -> 1.0]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `find_minimum`, `rewrite`
